    "source_id": "companion:pbps-conditional-c1-resolvent",
    "anchor": "PBPS arXiv:2609.06905v1 Appendix C.1 proof of Lemma B.1/Lemma C.1 compact-smooth-to-weighted-H1 analytic prerequisite; Section2.2 equations2.6-2.14 actual reflected conditional law. SPHMC2609.06906v1 Section4.1 BL actual-resolvent dependency only.",
    "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A3.SS1",
    "original_text": "Explicit analytic prerequisite restatement:\nE has the same full-space finite-dimensional real Hilbert/Borel structure, including dimension zero. V is C2 with true all-point/all-direction alpha I<=Hess V<=beta I, alpha,beta NNReal, 0<alpha<=beta, eta>0 and beta eta<=1.\nThe original Gibbs law, genuine independent Gaussian augmentation, selected R,S kernels, reflected W_y, finite positive partition and fixed original gradient D per fiber are derived by the existing actual conditional producer. Neither normalization nor a convenient replacement operator is supplied.\nThe potential is reflected, with quarter Hessian scaling. The unreflected SPHMC RGO potential/law is different. Existence is fiberwise for every y; no joint measurable resolvent selection, unbounded cost transfer or macroscopic H1/Poincare theorem is asserted.\nFor actual C2 V with 0<alpha<=beta global Hessian bounds, eta>0 and beta eta<=1, construct the actual Gibbs-Gaussian augmentation and common Markov conditional kernels R,S, with disintegration R and S_y=(R_y)#(x->2x-y). S_y is the true normalized reflected Gibbs law for W_y(u)=V((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta), with C2 regularity and positive integrable weight. For every y, retain one dense closable exact compact-smooth gradient D, fixed before epsilon/input, and derive every positive-epsilon L2 forcing weak solution, ordinary weak gradient/local integrability and all C1 compact weighted volume test equations. No measurable solution selection in y is claimed.\nSame actual compact-gradient graph closure admits C1 compact function/gradient pairs; actual positive-epsilon weak resolvent has all C1 compact weighted volume tests and genuine ordinary weak gradient. Actual PBPS reflected conditional R/S law and original fixed D precede epsilon/input. No local H2, global operator-core/Bochner, conditional Poincare/BL, centered epsilon limit, noncompact constant/linear domains, measurable y-selection, SPHMC Hessian lower/full4.1, PBPS hypocoercivity or either complete main/composition. TV never transfers unbounded expected cost.",
    "text_sha256": "31bb04cef2362d549bbfa8c37debeca0249ca718eb691dcc551038101e17149c"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.ExampleCases.ProximalBPS.ConditionalC1Resolvent.conditional_c1_resolvent",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/ExampleCases/ProximalBPS/ConditionalC1Resolvent.lean",
    "statement": "{E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [InnerProductSpace ℝ E]\n    [FiniteDimensional ℝ E] [MeasurableSpace E] [BorelSpace E]\n    {V : E → ℝ} {α β : NNReal} {η : ℝ}\n    (hα : 0 < (α:ℝ)) (hαβ : α ≤ β) (hV : ContDiff ℝ 2 V)\n    (hH : ∀ x v : E, (α:ℝ)*‖v‖^2 ≤ (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ∧\n      (fderiv ℝ (fderiv ℝ V) x v) v ≤ (β:ℝ)*‖v‖^2)\n    (hη : 0 < η) (hβη : (β:ℝ)*η ≤ 1) :\n    let μ := (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -V x)\n    let J := Measure.map (fun p : E × E => (p.1,p.1+Real.sqrt η • p.2)) (μ.prod (stdGaussian E))\n    let W := fun y u : E => V ((1/2:ℝ) • (y+u)) + ‖u-y‖^2/(8*η)\n    ∃ R S : Kernel E E, IsMarkovKernel R ∧ IsMarkovKernel S ∧\n      (J.map Prod.swap).IsCondKernel R ∧\n      (∀ y, S y = (R y).map (fun x => (2:ℝ) • x-y)) ∧\n      ∀ y, S y = (volume : Measure E).tilted (fun u => -W y u) ∧\n        ContDiff ℝ 2 (W y) ∧ Integrable (fun u => Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        0 < (∫ u, Real.exp (-W y u)) ∧\n        ∃ D : Lp ℝ 2 (S y) →ₗ.[ℝ] Lp E 2 (S y),\n          Dense (D.domain : Set (Lp ℝ 2 (S y))) ∧ D.IsClosable ∧ D.closure.IsClosed ∧\n          (∀ (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) (v : Lp E 2 (S y)), (u,v) ∈ D.graph ↔\n            ∃ f : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ ∞ f ∧ HasCompactSupport f ∧\n              u =ᵐ[S y] f ∧ v =ᵐ[S y] gradient f) ∧\n      ∀ (ε : ℝ), 0 < ε → ∀ f : Lp ℝ 2 (S y),\n      ∃ u : D.closure.domain,\n        (∀ v : D.closure.domain,\n          ε * ⟪(u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)), (v : Lp ℝ 2 (S y))⟫ +\n            ⟪D.closure u, D.closure v⟫ = ⟪f, (v : Lp ℝ 2 (S y))⟫) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x) ∧\n        LocallyIntegrable (fun x => D.closure u x) ∧\n        (∀ ψ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → HasCompactSupport ψ → ∀ v : E,\n          Integrable (fun x => ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n          (∫ x, ψ x * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) v) =\n            - ∫ x, (u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * fderiv ℝ ψ x v) ∧\n        ∀ ψ : E → ℝ, ContDiff ℝ 1 ψ → HasCompactSupport ψ →\n          Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W y x) * ((u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * ψ x)) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W y x) * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) (gradient ψ x)) ∧\n          Integrable (fun x => Real.exp (-W y x) * (f x * ψ x)) ∧\n          ε * (∫ x, Real.exp (-W y x) * ((u : Lp ℝ 2 (S y)) x * ψ x)) +\n            (∫ x, Real.exp (-W y x) * inner ℝ (D.closure u x) (gradient ψ x)) =\n            ∫ x, Real.exp (-W y x) * (f x * ψ x)",
    "statement_sha256": "6a7e722218a5242fe87e07a994e6196de7feae82af3dfffea3cc23cc48bd4ba3",
    "compiled": true,
    "formalizer": "root-samplinglib-writer",
    "decoder_context": [
      "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its Borel measurable space and canonical Lebesgue volume, including dimension zero. All section ambient instances remain part of the contract. NNReal denotes nonnegative real scalars.",
      "Lp F 2 mu is the actual L2 quotient space; MemLp means a measurable representative with finite L2 norm. MemLp.toLp embeds the actual function class and agrees mu-a.e. Inner products of L2 classes integrate pointwise real inner products against mu.",
      "ContDiff R 1 means C1; infinity means smooth. gradient f is the Riesz representative of the actual Frechet derivative fderiv R f. HasCompactSupport means the topological closure of nonzero support is compact.",
      "LinearPMap is a real-linear partial operator on its stated submodule domain. Its graph consists of pairs of a domain element and its actual output. D.IsClosable means its topological graph closure is single-valued; D.closure is that same closed operator. Coercions from its domain and from L2 classes choose the usual representatives. No test membership is built into these definitions.",
      "Measure.tilted f is exp(f)/integral exp(f) times the original measure. Probability/nonzero normalization is not built into this definition. Kernel is a measurable probability-transition family when IsMarkovKernel holds. A conditional kernel disintegrates the specified joint measure; measure.map is actual pushforward and prod is the actual independent product. stdGaussian denotes the standard real Hilbert Gaussian. All volume or law integrals specify their actual measure."
    ],
    "compiler_evidence": "Focused production3303/Test3305 PASS, actual nonquadratic conditional and compact C1 observable, standard3 only. Separate full mathematics/blind/source/exactcommit/integration pending."
