    "statement": "For actual C2 V with 0<alpha<=beta global Hessian bounds, eta>0 and beta eta<=1, construct the actual Gibbs-Gaussian augmentation and common Markov conditional kernels R,S, with disintegration R and S_y=(R_y)#(x->2x-y). S_y is the true normalized reflected Gibbs law for W_y(u)=V((y+u)/2)+norm(u-y)^2/(8eta), with C2 regularity and positive integrable weight. For every y, retain one dense closable exact compact-smooth gradient D, fixed before epsilon/input, and derive every positive-epsilon L2 forcing weak solution, ordinary weak gradient/local integrability and all C1 compact weighted volume test equations. No measurable solution selection in y is claimed.",
